{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228475Z","id":"ed3d25a396997edc5d24d713df2869ea9b61d04d5db6a66e02a902603f5e2935","body":{"detail":"Spec section 11 says the agent side sends repo and branch on registration. join() posts harness, pids, cwd, transcript_path and codex_home only; crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:507-524 renames a hook's row once the shim joins with a repository (crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs:73). Until then People, the roster and the Send menu show the agent as 'claude' or 'codex', and an agent that never starts its MCP server (or a script such as scripts/dev-second-person.sh, which registers through the hook alone) keeps that name. clax_core::names::repo_and_branch reads git files without a git process, so the hook can call it on the input's cwd.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"f87fcd7851c58ecefae80aeee26f3c2499abe1391cd04bba2ae43a8ce9fb0387"},"suggested_fix":"In join(), add repo and branch from clax_core::names::repo_and_branch(Path::new(cwd)) when the input has a cwd, and test that a hook-only registration from a repository gets the derived name.","summary":"A hook's session join sends no repo or branch, so an agent registered by its SessionStart hook is named after its harness until its MCP shim joins","tags":["review","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/ask.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.169908Z","id":"73ffc4d27bd57563a65d1795f1d771a38b6553cee083adcb921aea4b1e6cb5d6","body":{"detail":"On a home connected with clax connect (remote.json), `clax hook --agent claude ask` with an AskUserQuestion PreToolUse input exits 0 with no output and logs 'ask mode=- outcome=error waited_s=0' in the home's hook log, so the terminal dialog opens even while the person's browser holds the questions topic. Seen on a scratch daemon bound to 0.0.0.0 with the person's agent registered by `clax hook --agent claude session-start`; the same person's agent asking through `clax mcp`'s ask tool reaches the person's inbox card and gets the answer (web/e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts). try_ask returns the error before choosing a mode: live_session or the question POST fails for the remote client.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"49e4c159ec3770ff579ab3b183a3f5cce8d9dc834b2c52421f1b6c182415311b"},"suggested_fix":"Make the remote hook find its session and post the question signed as the machine (the plan's remote_hooks_find_their_session), then add a person's hook question to web/e2e/inbox-cards.spec.ts.","summary":"A connected person's Claude Code AskUserQuestion is not mirrored into their inbox: the remote hook's ask ends in an error","tags":["task:19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.738022Z","id":"ab5da9d5521a26999f245d9cf9184d5ad88c8036122f9a4811f36d72681b12db","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"join() sends repo and branch from clax_core::names::repo_and_branch(cwd); the store names a row the join makes, or a hook's row named from its harness alone, after them; an older daemon refusing the fields is asked again without them. Evidence: events::tests::a_join_sends_the_repository_and_branch_of_its_cwd and store::sessions::tests::names::a_hooks_join_names_its_row_after_the_repository pass, and each fails with its half removed.","supersedes":"ed3d25a396997edc5d24d713df2869ea9b61d04d5db6a66e02a902603f5e2935","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/ask.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.738883Z","id":"36f61b79ffe897984518e377e1baf4850a4fc0ec193b9d247305f60339b7f9d1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"With per-session proofs (the hook names its session with X-Clax-Session and its secret from the credential file) the remote hook's ask mirrors the question. Evidence: connect::a_remote_hooks_ask_mirrors_the_question (no surface open: outcome=terminal, question recorded for Sam's session) and connect::a_remote_hooks_ask_waits_for_the_persons_answer (Sam's browser holds the questions topic; the hook waits and hands Claude Code his answer) pass.","supersedes":"73ffc4d27bd57563a65d1795f1d771a38b6553cee083adcb921aea4b1e6cb5d6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320244Z","id":"e79206868b4ee5bf2bd63a5ab4e6d6f4cca7e3410252e2e85ce81851c42fc05c","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"16191800fd69c7416b72cd8546872a1a2a4f6e7394c835b5adc468a3ddd90a5a"},"summary":"feedback_text's doc says the text is passed through unchanged, but it now goes through Daemon::agent_text, which rewrites a remote daemon's clips","tags":["review","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.441491Z","id":"ac4cf5c64340140954c71027ff3cec38f24d397988a6eebb15cafba580e1ccb5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"The doc now says the text goes through Daemon::agent_text (7a06e2cd).","supersedes":"e79206868b4ee5bf2bd63a5ab4e6d6f4cca7e3410252e2e85ce81851c42fc05c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T02:12:18.859454Z","id":"271c2d23bf00b398e218f2f3e73bdf5ca06e4e940b29eeaefaa873731cc62452","body":{"detail":"unwoken() counts every watch with replies armed, and publishing watches the artifact with replies armed (crates/clax-core/src/store/watches.rs ensure_watch_in). So a Claude Code, Codex or Grok session that publishes once, with no channel, follower or codex queue, has its next stop blocked once with the follower commands, even when the person never asked to iterate on the page. Current behaviour: count them (the Claude Code skill already told agents to start a follower after the first publish). Option: count only watches made by the watch tool (the watches table's source column is 'direct' for those) and live-page watches, and leave a publish's watch to the skill text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":427},"content_hash":"a9c48bfd23032b7d11ec20eff400dbc68bd3524847ee705a2e3ec3da065aca87"},"summary":"Watches that publish made count toward the Stop hook's one-time 'nothing wakes this session' block","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T02:12:18.859572Z","id":"bbd7607bbea7d1895afbdf494a48565595af3f035384ef832343a808d248ab02","body":{"detail":"For harness codex with push unavailable (codex not on the daemon's PATH, CLAX_CODEX_BIN empty, or no Codex session ID), unwoken() blocks one stop per watch arming with the wake block's do (crates/clax-core/src/wake.rs, the (\"codex\", _) branch): nothing the agent can start would wake Codex, so the block's only effect is that the agent tells the person 'Codex can't be woken here; running codex queue ... needs codex on the Clax daemon's PATH'. Current behaviour: block once. Option: never block Codex, and rely on the watch result's wake and the SessionStart Push: line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":405},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"ebaff57047402a9e59ec27d6baa20a19da863104cc407d9bdca41d6d124b77eb"},"summary":"A Codex session codex queue cannot reach has one stop blocked only so it tells the person","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.340374Z","id":"97e22f80508140c0225ddc4a55c16095da3b4d4423efe1ac2ed8628161b5fe83","body":{"detail":"For harness codex with push unavailable (codex not on the daemon's PATH, CLAX_CODEX_BIN empty, or no Codex session ID), unwoken() blocks one stop per watch arming with the wake block's do (crates/clax-core/src/wake.rs, the (\"codex\", _) branch): nothing the agent can start would wake Codex, so the block's only effect is that the agent tells the person 'Codex can't be woken here; running codex queue ... needs codex on the Clax daemon's PATH'. Current behaviour: block once. Option: never block Codex, and rely on the watch result's wake and the SessionStart Push: line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"ebaff57047402a9e59ec27d6baa20a19da863104cc407d9bdca41d6d124b77eb"},"summary":"A Codex session codex queue cannot reach has one stop blocked only so it tells the person","supersedes":"bbd7607bbea7d1895afbdf494a48565595af3f035384ef832343a808d248ab02","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.352686Z","id":"134d9b31665465c5f7121916f9d666a82ea479c99a0a82a7f01f733d6ad5621d","body":{"detail":"unwoken() counts every watch with replies armed, and publishing watches the artifact with replies armed (crates/clax-core/src/store/watches.rs ensure_watch_in). So a Claude Code, Codex or Grok session that publishes once, with no channel, follower or codex queue, has its next stop blocked once with the follower commands, even when the person never asked to iterate on the page. Current behaviour: count them (the Claude Code skill already told agents to start a follower after the first publish). Option: count only watches made by the watch tool (the watches table's source column is 'direct' for those) and live-page watches, and leave a publish's watch to the skill text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":435},"content_hash":"a9c48bfd23032b7d11ec20eff400dbc68bd3524847ee705a2e3ec3da065aca87"},"summary":"Watches that publish made count toward the Stop hook's one-time 'nothing wakes this session' block","supersedes":"271c2d23bf00b398e218f2f3e73bdf5ca06e4e940b29eeaefaa873731cc62452","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-hooks/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.619048Z","id":"80246ed51e5ef550789ddf6c040d8f3a5f40c3770b6037f28899e87cee7a34ab","body":{"detail":"prompt() polls tier=prompt_hook&prompt=true, which records the person's prompt as terminal activity and lapses the session's open hook in-terminal questions. Locally this is covered by crates/clax-server/tests/api_where_to_ask.rs the_prompt_hooks_poll_records_the_prompt_and_says_where_to_ask (line 352) and claude_codes_prompt_hook_records_the_prompt_and_lapses_an_in_terminal_question (line 672). Against a remote, crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come (line 1799) runs the prompt hook but asserts only its feedback text; a_remote_hooks_ask_mirrors_the_question (line 1421) and a_remote_hooks_ask_waits_for_the_persons_answer (line 1561) cover the ask hook only. Nothing checks that a connected person's prompt reaches their remote's where-to-ask signals. (Record 73ffc4d2, the remote AskUserQuestion failure, is resolved by 36f61b79.)","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":536},"end":{"line":547},"content_hash":"54baf651dc1f49c7c051c9780b3971ad6e51ec3304290250545903588a2f3a51"},"suggested_fix":"In crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs, run the prompt hook on the person's machine and assert GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask on the remote reports terminal_at.","summary":"The prompt hook's prompt=true report is untested against a remote (connected) daemon","tags":["test-gap","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
